This document describes the core features of Monta’s Charge Point Management System (Monta Hub) and the end-user mobile app (Monta Charge). 

***Monta Hub – CPMS Backend***
Charge Point & Hardware management: 
Centralized control of charger configuration, status monitoring, and firmware updates.

Fleet Integration: 
Connect and manage vehicles, usage tracking, smart scheduling, and centralised reporting for fleet charging
activities.

Home Charging Reimbursement: 
Automates reimbursement for home charging and energy use tracking.

Pricing Configuration: 
Admins can set flexible pricing models per location, time of day, or customer group.

User Access & Role Management: 
Define roles for admins, operators, or partners with custom permissions.

Live Monitoring & Alerts: 
Real-time overview of Charge Point status, live usage, and issue alerts.

Reports & Analytics: 
Exportable insights on energy usage, revenue, user behavior, and station health.

Settlement & Invoicing: 
Tools for handling payments, commissions, and reconciliation between partners.

***Monta Charge - End User Mobile App***
Charge Point Search: 
Allows users to find available public or private charging stations nearby or at a specified location.

Start/Stop Charging Sessions:
Users can initiate or stop charging with one tap, either via QR scan or remote control through the app.

Payment Integration:
Multiple payment options supported (credit card, Apple Pay, Google Pay) with transparent pricing.

Charge History:
Access to previous charging sessions, including time, location, energy used, and cost.

Favorites & Home Charging:
Mark preferred stations, manage home charger connectivity, and monitor usage.

User Profiles & Roles:
Account management including family/organization sharing options.

Support & Helpdesk access:
In-app support channels, FAQs, and contact features to reach the Operator’s support.


